  "description": "Each direction's stamps never decrease, across a core restart included (immortality §4.2, LOCKED: timestamps are worker-owned; decision 5.22: the worker stamps at read time, the core preserves the stamp). Each stamp keeps its owner: the worker keeps a session's output stamps non-decreasing at the source — here its clock stepped back between output 3 and 4, and it stamped 4 with 3's value, never a smaller one — and the core never alters an output stamp, so the replayed output 4 carries the stamp run 1 tapped; the core keeps its own input stamps non-decreasing the same way. Across directions nothing is assumed: input 3 is stamped before output 5 by another clock. Captures of a real run must hold the same.",
